---
import {
  AiChat02Icon,
  Analytics01Icon,
  McpServerIcon,
  SearchList01Icon,
} from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
import FeaturePage from '@/components/FeaturePage.astro'

const related = [
  { title: 'ChatGPT', text: 'Add SEO Skill to ChatGPT as a custom MCP server.', href: '/integrations/chatgpt', icon: McpServerIcon },
  { title: 'seo report', text: 'The Search Console report ChatGPT reads first.', href: '/docs/report', icon: Analytics01Icon },
  { title: 'seo research', text: 'Keyword data, and whether ChatGPT search cites your site.', href: '/docs/research', icon: SearchList01Icon },
  { title: 'AI search tracking', text: 'The questions people ask AI that show in your Search Console.', href: '/features/ai-search', icon: AiChat02Icon },
]
---

<FeaturePage
  title="ChatGPT SEO with your own search data"
  description="Use ChatGPT for SEO with your real Search Console, Google Analytics and keyword data through a free MCP server. Setup steps, prompts and what it can check."
  path="/features/chatgpt-seo"
  lead="ChatGPT can write a decent SEO plan from memory. Connect your Search Console and it writes one for your site, from your own clicks, queries and pages."
  {related}
>
  <h2>Why ChatGPT needs your data for SEO</h2>
  <p>
    Prompt lists for ChatGPT SEO work on the text you paste in. They can't see
    which queries you rank on page two for, which pages lost their clicks, or
    whether Google still has a page in its index. SEO Skill gives ChatGPT
    those facts from your own Search Console, Google Analytics and URL
    Inspection, so its answer starts from your numbers.
  </p>

  <h2>Add SEO Skill to ChatGPT</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Plugins, choose +, then Add custom MCP server.</li>
    <li>Name it seoskill and enter <code>https://seoskill.dev/mcp</code> under Connection.</li>
    <li>Choose OAuth for authentication, confirm, and choose Create as a plugin. Sign in with Google when ChatGPT asks. Access is read only.</li>
    <li>In a chat, type @ and pick seoskill.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Custom MCP servers depend on your ChatGPT plan. OpenAI lists Business,
    Enterprise and Edu workspaces, where an admin may need to create the
    plugin, and Pro accounts for read-only servers like this one. The <a href="/integrations/chatgpt">ChatGPT setup page</a> has the current
    steps.
  </p>

  <h2>Prompts to try in ChatGPT</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Ask</th><th>What ChatGPT reads</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Give me three quick wins for my site.</td><td>Queries close to page one (<a href="/features/striking-distance-keywords">striking distance keywords</a>) and pages with a low click-through rate for their position.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Which pages are losing traffic?</td><td>Content decay and traffic drops from Search Console, page by page.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Is this page indexed?</td><td>Google's URL Inspection result and the live page facts.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>How much traffic do AI assistants send us?</td><td>Visits from ChatGPT, Perplexity and others in Google Analytics or Clicky.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Does ChatGPT search cite us for our top questions?</td><td>Your top AI-style questions from Search Console, asked on ChatGPT search with your DataForSEO key.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool ChatGPT calls is free with no usage cap. Keyword research and
    the AI answer check use your own DataForSEO or Ahrefs key, so you pay that
    provider directly (a full AI answer check is about 7 cents of DataForSEO
    credit). The weekly site audit is $50 a month per site.
  </p>
</FeaturePage>
